(885036, 99020, 16301, '<td valign="top">I like the idea and message in this photo. I think a B&amp;W would have looked good to even out the skin tones, or desaturate the greens/yellows?. Gave it a 7, keep it up...</td>', 'I like the idea and message in this photo. I think a B&W would have looked good to even out the skin tones, or desaturate the greens/yellows?. Gave it a 7, keep it up...', '2004-08-31 04:34:40.000000', NULL, 0),
(885054, 99246, 8522, '<td valign="top">I didn''t tick Konador''s comment below, as the title I chose for this photo was supposed to have a certain irony to it... traditionally you say ''sweet dreams'' to children before they go to sleep and dream of nice fluffy things, this picture has more of an edge to it!<br/>I think this irony may have been lost on many people.<br/>I understand that the red was not for everyone, but I find the colour quite ''primal'', and Dr. Jones'' comment realised a little of my intention when he said it had a peep-show element to it. That wasn''t quite what I was aiming for, but I do think that this deep red has a certain link to an instinctive animal sexuality... or at least that''s what I was aiming for.<br/>I''ll never figure out DPC though, I thought this would get a higher score than 5.2, but I really like my shot and stand by it.</td>', 'I didn''t tick Konador''s comment below, as the title I chose for this photo was supposed to have a certain irony to it... traditionally you say ''sweet dreams'' to children before they go to sleep and dream of nice fluffy things, this picture has more of an edge to it!I think this irony may have been lost on many people.I understand that the red was not for everyone, but I find the colour quite ''primal'', and Dr. Jones'' comment realised a little of my intention when he said it had a peep-show element to it. That wasn''t quite what I was aiming for, but I do think that this deep red has a certain link to an instinctive animal sexuality... or at least that''s what I was aiming for.I''ll never figure out DPC though, I thought this would get a higher score than 5.2, but I really like my shot and stand by it.', '2004-08-31 06:17:18.000000', NULL, 0),
(885077, 98655, 18349, '<td valign="top">I said it before, and I''ll say it again... <br/> <br/><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by laurielblack:</b></div><hr/><i> This is a beautiful example of how lighting makes or breaks a portrait., and of how attractive the lines and form of a man''s body can be.   Very well executed photograph.  I am impressed.  :o) </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Wow...can''t believe this didn''t ribbon.  Remarkable image.  :o)</td>', 'I said it before, and I''ll say it again...  Originally posted by laurielblack: This is a beautiful example of how lighting makes or breaks a portrait., and of how attractive the lines and form of a man''s body can be.   Very well executed photograph.  I am impressed.  :o)   Wow...can''t believe this didn''t ribbon.  Remarkable image.  :o)', '2004-08-31 07:17:24.000000', NULL, 0),
(885154, 99123, 3084, '<td valign="top">When I judged all of the images submitted for the Nude II challenge, this submission stood out far and above the rest.  It was my pick for the challenge.  Terrific work, I am happy for you that everyone else saw its creative value too.  You have a great eye for lighting and composition.</td>', 'When I judged all of the images submitted for the Nude II challenge, this submission stood out far and above the rest.  It was my pick for the challenge.  Terrific work, I am happy for you that everyone else saw its creative value too.  You have a great eye for lighting and composition.', '2004-08-31 08:49:17.000000', NULL, 0),
