(889808, 99418, 24169, '<td valign="top"><b>Critique Club Comment:</b> <br/> <br/>Congrats on being in the top 20!<br/> <br/>It''s a fun photo with good colours but there are a few more comments I''d like to make:<br/> <br/> - The right hand side does seem to be a little brighter than the left and there is also a bit of brightness by the knees in both poses. <br/> <br/> - Could have possibly been a bit sharper, esp around the faces.<br/> <br/> - Composition could have been slightly better - maybe a little more space between the two poses as they feel a bit close. <br/> <br/>All in all, I think it''s a wonderful photo; inovative and well executed.</td>', 'Critique Club Comment:  Congrats on being in the top 20! It''s a fun photo with good colours but there are a few more comments I''d like to make:  - The right hand side does seem to be a little brighter than the left and there is also a bit of brightness by the knees in both poses.   - Could have possibly been a bit sharper, esp around the faces.  - Composition could have been slightly better - maybe a little more space between the two poses as they feel a bit close.  All in all, I think it''s a wonderful photo; inovative and well executed.', '2004-09-02 14:03:19.000000', NULL, 0),
(889839, 99247, 772, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club :)<br/> <br/>Hi Nathaliedoo...<br/> <br/>This is a beautiful composition.  I absolutely love everything about the view you chose here.  The high key nautre of it works fairly well also.  I think this is an excellent canditate for black and white because the colors within the image don''t work particularly well for me.  There is not enough color to provide any significant strength, and the image almost appears monochromatic by nature.  The color within the image also doesn''t seem to mesh well with your choice of border colors.  That particular combination, to me, just feels bland.  I think this image, converted to black and white would have a nice gallery quality feel to it if the pink part of the border was also changed to black.  <br/> <br/>Added: After reading the comments you received, I rememberd that I did a high key ''minimal'' image for this challenge as well.  That concept doesn''t seem to do well here at DPC.  The voters here aren''t used to seeing it and don''t give it a ''chance'' to be absorbed for what it is.  There are a few who recognize the merit in it, but I was definitely surprised at how few...<br/> <br/>Excellent work :)<br/> <br/>John Setzler<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2004-09-02 13:44:59.</i></td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club :) Hi Nathaliedoo... This is a beautiful composition.  I absolutely love everything about the view you chose here.  The high key nautre of it works fairly well also.  I think this is an excellent canditate for black and white because the colors within the image don''t work particularly well for me.  There is not enough color to provide any significant strength, and the image almost appears monochromatic by nature.  The color within the image also doesn''t seem to mesh well with your choice of border colors.  That particular combination, to me, just feels bland.  I think this image, converted to black and white would have a nice gallery quality feel to it if the pink part of the border was also changed to black.   Added: After reading the comments you received, I rememberd that I did a high key ''minimal'' image for this challenge as well.  That concept doesn''t seem to do well here at DPC.  The voters here aren''t used to seeing it and don''t give it a ''chance'' to be absorbed for what it is.  There are a few who recognize the merit in it, but I was definitely surprised at how few... Excellent work :) John Setzler', '2004-09-02 14:42:56.000000', '2004-09-02 14:44:59.000000', 0),
(889928, 99247, 10686, '<td valign="top">I really like this too, I gave it an 8. <br/> <br/>I like the light color, but agree with John that B&amp;W has potential too.  <br/> <br/>You may have tried this, but the darker areas may be just a bit on the light side. Consider adding some more contrast to do that. <br/> <br/></td>', 'I really like this too, I gave it an 8.  I like the light color, but agree with John that B&W has potential too.   You may have tried this, but the darker areas may be just a bit on the light side. Consider adding some more contrast to do that.  ', '2004-09-02 15:45:37.000000', NULL, 0),
(889981, 98721, 6999, '<td valign="top"><b>From the Critique Club</b> <br/> <br/>It would be pointless of me to make remarks about any percieved technical problems with this shot - you''re good enough to get this far, you''re good enough to know for yourself what you like/don''t like and why about it.<br/> <br/>I''m no fan of hyper-stylised posed photography, nor of most studio work, but I have written what I think before on a couple of ribbon-winning shots and got slated for it, so am going to add nothing more.<br/> <br/>Your ribbon must be your critique, I fear.<br/> <br/>E</td>', 'From the Critique Club  It would be pointless of me to make remarks about any percieved technical problems with this shot - you''re good enough to get this far, you''re good enough to know for yourself what you like/don''t like and why about it. I''m no fan of hyper-stylised posed photography, nor of most studio work, but I have written what I think before on a couple of ribbon-winning shots and got slated for it, so am going to add nothing more. Your ribbon must be your critique, I fear. E', '2004-09-02 16:32:48.000000', NULL, 0),
(890024, 98120, 14773, '<td valign="top">Aside from it not being a nude photo, I completely disagree with most of the comments made about this.  It''s a great photo, I like the contrast-y lighting and I LOVE the pose and environment!  Not to mention cudos to the stylist, she looks great.  You know, I''ve worked with some great stylists, models and other very talented people, and I still think this is a great/unique photo.</td>', 'Aside from it not being a nude photo, I completely disagree with most of the comments made about this.  It''s a great photo, I like the contrast-y lighting and I LOVE the pose and environment!  Not to mention cudos to the stylist, she looks great.  You know, I''ve worked with some great stylists, models and other very talented people, and I still think this is a great/unique photo.', '2004-09-02 17:15:03.000000', NULL, 0),
(890436, 99365, 3548, '<td valign="top">I like it alot, claudia. Shedding a little light on the "dark side," eh?!   In fact, had you cropped it slightly more, or had your model keep his knees together a little tighter, you could have had a rather hairy cross -- possibly, even, an ankh. In any case, an interesting comment on the unconscious or dark side of  a certain western religion. Way to go!<br/> <br/></td>', 'I like it alot, claudia. Shedding a little light on the "dark side," eh?!   In fact, had you cropped it slightly more, or had your model keep his knees together a little tighter, you could have had a rather hairy cross -- possibly, even, an ankh. In any case, an interesting comment on the unconscious or dark side of  a certain western religion. Way to go! ', '2004-09-02 23:43:11.000000', NULL, 0),
